\section*{A universal joint critical SK equilibrium and quench autocorrelation law}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
The linked manuscripts present the following claims by OpenAI: Critical stationary SK autocorrelation is claimed to have a common random functional limit for Gaussian and sign couplings after time scaling by $n^{2/3}$ and amplitude by $n^{1/3}$; The critical SK quench from independent fair spins is claimed to share a functional scaling law for Gaussian and sign couplings and to relax to the stationary limit at long waiting times. Together they give a claimed affirmative answer in the matching scope.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
A conditioned spectral-edge measure and quantitative observation estimates control variance at the cap scale. Microscopic relaxation identifies the effective coefficient, resolvent-trace convergence yields the Gaussian process limit, and coupling comparison transports it to sign disorder.

Bottom-edge Gaussian estimates control warming on the critical clock. Positive-time limits select an entrance law from the uniform initial state, while smooth truncation of dynamical histories permits disorder replacement; comparison with the stationary edge input identifies the eventual relaxation.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The source identifies the equilibrium autocorrelation process A. The joint quench B, entrance densities and waiting-time relaxation are additional requirements. The critical SK quench from independent fair spins is claimed to share a functional scaling law for Gaussian and sign couplings and to relax to the stationary limit at long waiting times. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 227, the selected statements include the high-temperature gap for $\beta<1$, cutoff ratios only for $\beta<1/2$, critical lower mixing scales with a subexponential upper bound, and low-temperature barriers. They do not provide the full critical exponent, the full cutoff location, or the newer autocorrelation limits. No Comparator is assigned to the selected manuscript here; the family page selects other papers or supporting statements. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

